Hi Ian,

Our house/office survived Hurricane Richard. So while it appears to have withstood  90+mph winds the experience hunkered down in a small interior bathroom was like being in a  earthquake for 3 hours with the building shaking and bucking.
The surrounding forest really took a hard hit however.

I back at trying to get some work accomplished with Deducer 0.4.2, but puzzled that the predicted values are quite a bit off from the actual values in the one data set I just ran.
In this case there was only a singe NA field.  I am assuming now that the relationship between the call frequencies of the bats FC is not linearly related to their size based on Forearm FA.

Any ideas on what other models could be run to better predict this?

